          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Broadly speaking,
            %strong conceptual completeness
            for a logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrine"} doctrine
            refers to the following statement: if an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpretation"} interpretation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1 \to T_2
            between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            of the doctrine induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
