          %h2#strong_conceptual_completeness_for_coherent_logic Strong conceptual completeness for coherent logic
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultracategory"}> Ultracategories
            , introduced by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Makkai87"} Makkai ‘87
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#thm:conc-compl-pretoposes"}
            to a
            %em strong conceptual completeness
            theorem for coherent logic. Intuitively, the category of models
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Pretop
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Mod}(P)= \mathbf{Pretop}(P, Set)
            of a (small) pretopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            can be endowed with the structure of an ultracategory by considering the usual notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultraproducts"} ultraproducts
            of models; this way, the pretopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            can be reconstructed up to equivalence by considering
            %em ultrafunctors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Mod}(P) \to Set
          %p
          #thm:strong-conc-compl.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Strong conceptual completeness for pretoposes)
            %p
              For every small pretopos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ev
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Ult
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ev
                    \\colon
                    P \to \mathbf{Ult}\big( \operatorname{Mod}(P) , Set \big)
            %p
              is an equivalence of categories, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Ult
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Ult}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of ultracategories, ultrafunctors, and transformations thereof.
          %p
            In other words,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizing+object"} dualizing object
            for a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+adjunction"} dual 2-adjunction
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Makkai+duality"} Makkai duality
